        "level_fit": 4,
        "notes": "F3.4 is only partly covered: the lesson says fuller context costs more and recall gets worse (context rot), and that a bigger window does not fix this, but it never states that a larger window still needs managing or that everything kept is re-sent on every call as a cost. No fact is stated wrongly. The lesson suits the learner well, building on the agent loop and defining token, context and window, but terms like compaction and context rot arrive quickly, and the 10-minute pacing is tight."
